bevy-horizon: say on stderr whether the Switch's depth passes use ZCULL

For mesa-switch (https://github.com/danfromtico/mesa-switch, by danfromtico and NaGaa95; MIT)
at 606441c9, after 0001-0009 (it reports on 0009's switch). scripts/build_nvk.sh applies it;
this text before the first "diff --git" line is ignored by git apply.

Nothing showed whether NVK uses ZCULL on the Switch. nouveau_horizon_add_zcull_info drops
nvhost's ZCULL description without a word if it fails a check; an image has somewhere to save
ZCULL only with the right usage and layout; and a pass uses ZCULL only if its view is the whole
image. So if changing ZCULL's direction (0009) changed no timing, a run couldn't tell "ZCULL is
off" from "ZCULL doesn't help". These lines on stderr, which bevy-horizon's log keeps, tell:
  - nvhost's description, accepted or rejected, with its values (for the first two devices);
  - for each depth image, the first pass with ZCULL that loads it, the first that clears it and
    the first of another kind, with the direction and the bytes saved; and the first pass
    without ZCULL, with the reason, in the order nvk_CmdBeginRendering tests them;
  - each change of direction from one pass with ZCULL to the next;
  - the first 8 loads of ZCULL saved with the other direction that 0009 clears instead.
At most 48 lines besides those 8, so a run's log stays short; a pass pays an atomic read or two.

